module
public import WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.EffectiveCartier
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Noetherian
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Stalk
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.Basic

/-! # The Cartier complement over its generic DVR stalk
Source: Stacks Project, Tag 01WQ. -/

@[expose] public section
universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

/-- The Cartier complement at its generic DVR stalk is the fraction-field spectrum.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 01WQ; step 1 of
lem-sbc-cartier-stalk-normalization-product.
(blueprint: lem-sbc-cartier-stalk-punctured-complement)

Proof: An effective Cartier centre is a closed immersion. At the image of its
integral generic point the quotient of the base stalk by its Cartier ideal is
its field stalk. Hence the ideal is the maximal ideal of R. Its generator is
a nonzerodivisor, so it is nonzero in the domain R. The inverse image of the
complement is consequently the punctured spectrum of the DVR. Localizing at
a uniformizer identifies this open, over Spec R, with Spec Frac R: every nonzero
element of R is a unit times a power of the uniformizer. The open immersion
Spec Frac R into Spec R factors the map to N through V, giving t. Its image
is exactly the inverse image of V, so the displayed square is cartesian.
This construction needs no cover, group action, or normalization. A field
cannot be the displayed DVR stalk with a Cartier centre through its closed
point, since a field has no proper ideal generated by a nonzerodivisor. -/
theorem cartier_stalk_punctured_complement
    {N : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian N] (V : N.Opens)
    (D : Scheme.{u}) (j : D ⟶ N) (hD : IsIntegral D)
    (hj : IsEffectiveCartierCenter j) (hV : ∀ z : N, z ∈ V ↔ z ∉ Set.range j)
    (η : D) (hη : IsGenericPoint η Set.univ)
    [IsDomain (N.presheaf.stalk (j η))]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing (N.presheaf.stalk (j η))] :
    let R := N.presheaf.stalk (j η)
    ∃ t : Spec (CommRingCat.of (FractionRing R)) ⟶ V.toScheme,
      IsPullback t (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R (FractionRing R))))
        V.ι (N.fromSpecStalk (j η)) := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
